<font class="pn-normal"><strong>***MEMBER CONDUCT*** </strong><br><br>
*****1.) For scheduled raids, all members 55+ that are ON-LINE are required to attend.&nbsp;Those that do not may recieve a penalty unless a valid reason for inattendance is given (if you really feel you can't attend due to other in game obligations, let the raid leader know, were not tyrants here). &nbsp;Those members under level 55 are not required to attend (but can if they want, and the raid does not have a level restriction), but must be ready to give aid if called upon by the raid leader, as lvling should be their primary concern. &nbsp;Anyone asked to come on a raid by the raid leader is required to attend the raid regardless of level unless they have a valid escuse.<br><br>
*****2.) Members are expected to treat their fellow members with respect. &nbsp;Any complaints about other members should be submitted to the IA Officer for review (not argued over guild chat).<br><br>
*****3.) Whining about loot will not be tolerated over guild chat. &nbsp;If you have a concern about your loot, please email to the IA officer or the raid cooridinator, explaining the reasons for your concern.<br><br>
*****4.) We do expect guild members to actively use the web page as a lot of useful information is posted there (raid calender, point database). &nbsp;As well, we do expect to keep their information updated and to participate in dialogues on the chat boards. <br><br>
*****5.) As a member of this guild, we have no requirements regarding time spent playing. &nbsp;The only exception to this is officers, as they are expected to contribute more than the average member. But due to the way the guild is set up, the more time you contribute the more you are going to get out of the guild. <br><br>
*****6.) Regarding officers, every officer will be held accountable for their duties by the entire guild. &nbsp;If you have a complaint about an officer, either due to not doing there job or treating you with disrespect, please do not hesitate to email the GM or IA officer. &nbsp;Officers are held to a higher standard than everyone else, and it is the responsibility of every member to make sure they are doing their job. <br><br>
***NOTE: these policies are subject to change. &nbsp;Any changes to guild policy regarding member conduct will be announced via the message board and motd before going into effect. <br><br><br>
<strong>***OFFICER POSITIONS*** </strong><br><br>
*****1.) Raid Coordinator - This officer is responsible for maintaining and updating the guild raid calender. &nbsp;Any requests for raids by members must be sent to this officer. &nbsp;This officer and the GM are the ONLY ones that can set up official guild raids (point raids). &nbsp;This officer is also responsible for making members aware of upcoming raids via the message board and the motd. &nbsp;All raids must be scheduled at least a week in advance. &nbsp;Finally, this officer is required to submit next weeks calender for approval to the GM. &nbsp;For scheduling epic mobs via member requests using points, this officer must notify the points officer after the raid is completed (successful or not). <br><br>
*****2.) Recruitment Officer (passive) - This officer is primarily responsible for applications via the webpage. &nbsp;They will process applications and contact possible members to set up raid invites. &nbsp;This officer will also be reuired to notify the points officer if the applicant was recommened by a member so bonus points can be attributed. &nbsp;In addition, this officer is responsible for keeping track of the probationary period for all prospects. &nbsp;Any questions regarding recruitment MUST go to one of the recruitment officers. <br><br>
*****3.) Recruitment Officer (active) - This officer is primarily responsible for hunting out possible member prospects and inviting them to raids/guild events. &nbsp;Though all members are encouraged to recruit, this officer will be required to invite a minimum of five prospects a month. &nbsp;At the end of the month, a list of all players invited should be sent to the GM for verification. <br>Note: &nbsp;It is possible that this position will become obsolete after a period of time.<br><br>
*****4.) Point Officer: &nbsp;This officer is responsible for keeping track of points for all members. &nbsp;This will be done mostly via email from members and officers. &nbsp;This position requires a large amount of time to be done correctly! &nbsp;This officer will be required to update the point database at least twice a week, more if possible. &nbsp;Any negative points must be attributed immediately. &nbsp;Any questions regarding points will be decided by this officer and the GM ONLY. &nbsp;This officer will not distribute points, he will only keep track of the current points. &nbsp;Any Field Officer can distribute loot via the point system, but they are required to contact the points officer of what points were used and what points were gained by all members present. <br><br>
*****5.) Internal Affairs Officer - This officer is responsible for recieving all complaints about either members or officers for review. &nbsp;This officer can make a limited judgement on any situation and mete out disiciplinary action on a limited basis (deduction of points). &nbsp;Situations deemed too serious for point deduction must be passed onto the GM for a final decision. &nbsp;In addition, the parties involved can request to talk to the GM if they feel they are being treated unfairly. &nbsp;This officers must hear both sides of all complaints, and if deciding to take disciplinary action, must post on the message board his reasons for doing so. &nbsp;On any point deduction, the points officer must be contacted. &nbsp;Due to the sensitive nature of this position, the actions of this officer will be closely monitored. <br> Note: &nbsp;If a member wishes, any complaint can be kept anonymous (only the IA officer,GM, and the parties involved will know). <br><br>
*****6.) Morale Officer - It is the job of this officer to maintain the morale of the guild mainly through setting up guild events and other non-raid activities. &nbsp;This officer must be aware of current problems within the guild and try to rectify them before the IA officer has to get involved. &nbsp;For setting up events, this officer must work with the raid coordinator to set up dates. &nbsp;Differant activites at each event is a plus, so a creative mind will make this job easier. &nbsp;Essentially, it is the job of this officer to make sure everyone is having fun, and if they aren't, to find out why and let the GM know. &nbsp;Guild members are encouraged to talk to this officer or the IA officer if they are worried about guild affairs. &nbsp;All anonymity will be maintained for those that wish it. <br><br>
*****7.) Foreign Relations Officer - This officer will be responsible for achieving and maintaining alliances with other guilds. &nbsp;In addition, this officer should be actively working to increase our reputation on the server, via posting on CTC forums and news, smoothing over squabbles, as well as keeping our news page updated. &nbsp;This also involves taking pictures of guild events/raids for posting on our page and other eq sites.<br><br>
*****8,9.) Field Officers - One senior over the other, these are the officers that actually run the guild raids. &nbsp;They are responsible for organizing and executuing guild raids in game, working under the GM while he is present. &nbsp;In the absence of the GM, the senior Field Officer present has control of the raid. &nbsp;These officers are the ONLY ones who can distribute loot on official guild raids. &nbsp;As well, in the absence of the point officer, these officers are responsible for keeping track of attendance as well as points spent. <br><br><br>
<strong>***POINTS***</strong><br><br>
In Order of Oblivion, the majority of items are distributed via a &quot;points system.&quot; &nbsp;These points can be earned in a variety of ways: <br><br>
*****Guild Raids: These are raids oficially sanctioned by the GM and Raid Coordinator, on the Raid Calendar. &nbsp;Specific mobs that cannot be scheduled for will not be bound by this rule (The GM or Field Officer present will make the decision). &nbsp;Any raids put together by guild members spontaneiously will not be bound on the point system.<br>Note: A raid may consist of mutliple zones/mobs.<br><br>
*****Bonus Points: Points may be awarded by the GM for any actions deemed good or valorious. &nbsp;As well, officers will recieve bonus points for services to the guild (Their Job).&nbsp;&nbsp; <br>Note: These types of points are completely subjective, and amounts may change at any time.<br><br><br>
<strong>***BREAKDOWN OF THE POINTS SYSTEM*** </strong><br><br>
Gaining Points: <br><br>
*****1.) A maximum of ten points per day may be gained by every guild member. &nbsp;This rule will not be suspended for any reason. &nbsp;A day starts at twelve am. &nbsp;For raids, the points are attributed to the day the raid starts on. <br> Note: Bonus points are considered seperately from the daily points, and may succeed the 10 point daily maximum. <br><br>
*****2.) Raid Points: For guild members that are level 46 or above, 10 points will be given to members that arrive within 30 minutes of the raid start, and stay at least 2 hours or until the completion of the raid. &nbsp;For those members that arrive after the 30 minutes or leave before the completion and before 2 hours, half the amount will be given. &nbsp;The Field Officer in charge of the raid will decide when the official raid start is. <br>Note: It is your responsibility to check in and out with the officer taking attendence for the raid to recieve your points (generally the points officer). <br>Note: Some raids/zones may have a level restriction based on the type of mobs/agro/AE's in the zone. &nbsp;The level restriction will be decided by the Field Officer in charge of that raid, and noted on the raid calendar prior to the raid. &nbsp;Those members below the level requirement may be allowed on the raid if asked to come by the Field Officer, or if a personal request to attend is granted. <br><br>
Spending Points: <br><br>
*****1.) To buy an item on a raid, you must spend 1 point more than the next person that wants it. <br>Note: some items will not be buyable due to importance and will be awarded to a member based on what is most beneficial to the guild. &nbsp;For this to occur, the majority of officers on the raid must agree and must publicly state the reason for the decision. &nbsp;If a decision cannot be reached, the normal point system will apply. <br><br>
*****2.) You can also use your points to purchase a spot on the guild calender for personal quests (triggered mobs). &nbsp;The mob must be a triggered spawn, and the trigger mob must be up at the time of the raid. &nbsp;The member handing in the item to trigger the spawn will be awarded the loot from that mob. &nbsp;Currently, the amount of points required for this is 200, though this amount is subject to change. &nbsp;Any requests of this type must be submitted to the Raid Coordinator and is subject to Approval by the GM. <br> Note: &nbsp;Regardless of success or failure of the raid, points will be deducted from the members point total. &nbsp;If the trigger mob is not up (try to scout before we mobolize), points will not be deducted from the members point total. &nbsp;An attempt on the spawn must be made for points to be deducted. <br><br>****ANY ABUSE OF THE POINT SYSTEM WILL RESULT IN IMMEDIATE DE-GUILDING****&nbsp;&nbsp; <br><br><br>
<strong>***EPICS*** </strong><br><br>
To gain guild support for the completion of an epic, certain rules must be followed: <br><br> *****1.)Any member interested in completing their epic must post in the epic forum for their class the steps currently completed and the steps remaining. &nbsp;As well, please post whether each epic item is multi-questable or tradeable. <br><br>
*****2.) In the interest of completing as many epics as possible, the person farthest along and present (assuming it is not tradeable or multi-questable) will recieve the item. &nbsp;If the item can be traded or MQ'd, the member currently farthest along will recieve it, whether online or off. <br> Note: though you are not required to be present to recieve the epic item if you are farthest along, this is no excuse to not attend a raid that is set on the guild calendar that involves your item. &nbsp;If your on-line and not present, the item will go to the next person in line. <br> Note: If you are absent from game for a substantial period of time, epic items will go to the next person in the que. <br> Note: to be able to take advantage of this, you must submit your login/password to the GM, so he can log you on to recieve the item, otherwise no gaurantees can be made. <br><br>
*****3.) If two or more members are at the same bottleneck in their epics, the member that
was at the bottleneck first will recieve the epic item first. <br> Note: the queue for epics may switch if a members is surpassed by another in items required for completion. <br> Note: New members to the guild who are farther along on their epics will not go to the front of the list. &nbsp;They have to prove they are worthy of recieveing an epic and are here for the guild and not themselves before gaining support for an epic. <br> Note: If a member is absent from game for a substantial period of time, his place in the epic que may be reduced. <br><br><br>
<strong>***RECRUITMENT POLICY*** </strong><br><br>
All guild prospects must be equal to or above the average level of the current active level 50-60's in guild.(special cases may be made for people below this level). &nbsp;The average level will be posted in the recruitment forum. <br><br>
Prospects are expected to have these items before application: <br>1. Cobalt Scar Tooth <br>2. Trakanon Idol <br>3. Key to Charasis (Howling Stones) <br>4. Key to Skyshrine <br>5. Underwater breathing device (recommended but not required) <br>6. An instant unlimited single self buffing item (jboots, shrunken goblin earring, 8th coldain ring, etc.) (recommended but not required) <br>7. Prospects should also be working on gaining resist gear. <br><br>
*****1.) For those that wish to join OoO and do not have a sponsor, you must seek out an officer and express your desire to join the guild. &nbsp;You must notify the passive raid officer (noted under officer listing) and submit a formal application. &nbsp;Those that are most determined will have the best chance! <br><br>
*****2.) &nbsp;Prospects will become a probationary member for a duration of 3 weeks. &nbsp;During this 3 weeks, you are not eligible for loot, but can recieve points. &nbsp;This is your chance to show us the type of member you will be. &nbsp;Prospects are recommended to attend as many raids as they can as well as meet as many members as possible (Grouping works wonders!). &nbsp;Talk to the raid coordinator for information about upcoming raids. &nbsp;Those prospects that are most involved with the guild have the greatest chance of becoming full members. &nbsp;People who are joining just for loot will not be tolerated. <br><br><br>
<strong>***Prospect Probation Period***</strong><br><br>
At the end of the three week probation period, a vote will be held that is open to all full members to decide the outcome of the prospects membership. &nbsp;A minimum of 25 votes must be cast for the vote to be valid. &nbsp;If less than 25 votes are cast, the probationary period will be extended by one week, in order for the prospect to drum up support. &nbsp;After the one week period a second vote will be cast, if 25 votes are not cast then full membership will be denied. <br> Note: Any member who is 50+ may cast a Fatal vote against a member applying. &nbsp;As we value our current members over new applicants, any member has the ability to cast this fatal vote if the new applicant involved would cause serious problems in the guild. &nbsp;This fatal vote must be validated by the GM, and it is the GM's decision if the reasons stated for casting the vote are detremental enough to guild health to warrent not guilding the new applicant. &nbsp;Just not liking someone is not reason enough, as you can respect someone but still not like them, as long as you remain loyal to the idea of the guild as a whole. <br><br>
***If you do not attain membership your first time around, and still wish to join, you are welcome to apply again after 1 month***<br><br><br>
